File Title: Bodysize+movement.csv
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 This file contains a column header labelled 
\f0\b \'93Male ID\'94, 
\f2\b0 which was a unique identifier for an individual, consisting of an alphabetic prefix of \'93M\'94 followed by a Numerical identifier. The column named 
\f0\b Speaker Side
\f2\b0  records the side of the active speaker in a trial, which was randomly assigned to play a conspecific call from either the left or right side of the T-maze. Similarly, 
\f0\b Movement 
\f2\b0 records which side of the T maze the individual moved towards during the playback period. 
\f0\b Body size(mm)
\f2\b0  is the record of an individual\'92s body size, measured from the mandible to the tip of the abdomen. 
\f0\b Moved Towards 
\f2\b0 is a column with binary data which transforms the individual\'92s movement into a 1 if the male moved towards the speaker emitting playback, and 0 if the male moved away from or remained at the central position, using the Speaker Side and Movement data columns. 
\f0\b Moved Away
\f2\b0  is a binary data variable that indicates 1 if an individual moved away and 0 if they remained at the choice point (i.e., centre of the T maze, refer Figure 1 for details). 
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \

\f2 This file was used in determining whether a particular body-sized male moved towards an active speaker during the playback trials
\f1 \cf3 \ul \ulc3 [1]\cf2 \ulnone \'a0\cf3 \ul [2]\cf2 \ulnone \'a0
\f2 . The results and the graphical representation can be found in the supplementary file figure S2
\f1 \cf3 \ul [3]\cf2 \ulnone \'a0
\f2 .
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 File Title: Calling_effort.csv
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 This file contains a column header labelled 
\f0\b Audi_id,
\f2\b0  which contains the audio file names of the audio being used for the calling effort calculation. 
\f0\b Total_Gap_pre(s) 
\f2\b0 records the total amount of time an individual spent not calling during the 300-second pre-playback period. 
\f0\b Amount of time called(s)
\f2\b0  is calculated by subtracting Total_Gap_pre(s) from 300 seconds.
\f0\b  Calling_effort_pre_expo(proportion) 
\f2\b0 was calculated by dividing the Amount of time called(s) by 300. 
\f0\b Total_Gap_post(s) 
\f2\b0 records the total amount of time an individual spent not calling during the 300-second post-playback period.
\f0\b  Amount of time called(s)
\f2\b0  is calculated by subtracting Total_Gap_post(s) from 300 seconds.
\f0\b  Calling_effort_post(proportion) 
\f2\b0 was calculated by dividing the Amount of time called post-exposure (s) by 300. 
\f0\b Treatment 
\f2\b0 has the total information on the playback treatment duration of the trial, which can be 2, 5, or 10 minutes.
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \

\f2 Using this file, we determined whether calling effort changes after hearing a conspecific loud call for three different time intervals. The relevant analysis and the figure can be found in the main manuscript Result, Change In Call characteristics (SPL, CR, Calling Effort) section, Figure 7c. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 File Title: Exp2_null_movement.csv
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 This file contains a column header labelled 
\f0\b Trial Id 
\f2\b0 which records the trial ID. 
\f0\b Speaker side 
\f2\b0 refers to the side of the active speaker, which can be either left (L) or right (R). 
\f0\b Moving side 
\f2\b0 records which side of the T maze the individual moved towards before the playback period, for the first 10 minutes post release. 
\f0\b Movement 
\f2\b0 records whether the individual moved from the centre of the T-maze to either side. It is a binary data where if an individual moved to either side, it was noted as 1 and if it did not then 0. 
\f0\b Towards
\f2\b0  further filters the 
\f0\b Movement 
\f2\b0 column
\f0\b  
\f2\b0 into scoring males which moved towards the side of the active speaker as l and the rest as 0.
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \

\f2 Using this file, we determined whether the first 10 minutes of movement was an artefact of disturbance or was it an active movement towards the active speaker. The relevant analysis and the figure can be found in the Supplementary under S3. The Null Proportion\'a0of Movement\'a0\'a0along with the Figure S3.
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 File Title: Latency + Binary call data.csv 
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 This file contains a column header labelled 
\f0\b Trial
\f2\b0 , which records the trial ID. 
\f0\b Treatment 
\f2\b0 records the experiment type, which could be No Playback At Start or Playback At Start. 
\f0\b Latency 
\f2\b0 contains the information on the time it took an individual to initiate the call. 
\f0\b Call_no_call 
\f2\b0 contains the information on whether an individual called at all or remained silent throughout the experimental duration. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \

\f2 This file was used to plot and test whether individuals across treatments (No Playback at Start or Playback at Start) have a similar or different call latency distribution. The relevant analysis and the figure can be found in the main manuscript under the Results, 
\f3\i Call initiation
\f4  
\f2\i0 section along with the Figure 4a. 
\f1 \

\f2 It was also used in testing the call propensity of individuals within 10 minutes of release across treatments (No Playback At Start or Playback At Start; Supplementary). The relevant analysis and the figure can be found in the Supplementary under the section S4. The Null Proportion\'a0of Calling\'a0along with the Figure S4.
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 File Title: O.henryi_SPL_MovementALL_DATA_T1.csv
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 This file contains a column header labelled 
\f0\b DATE, 
\f2\b0 which stores the trial dates. 
\f0\b TRIAL_NO.
\f2\b0  contains the trial ID information, which is unique to each trial. 
\f0\b EXPOSURE(dB)
\f2\b0 \'a0 is the information of the decibel experienced by the cricket at the choice point, which was constant at 70 dB across and within the experiment type.
\f0\b  MALE_SPL_POST_EXPO(dB) 
\f2\b0 is the Sound Pressure Level (SPL) of a male post the cessation of the playback. Similarly, 
\f0\b CHIRP_RATE_POST_EXPO(s) 
\f2\b0 is the chirp rate of a male post-playback. 
\f0\b SPEAKER_SIDE 
\f2\b0 refers to the side of the active speaker, which can be either left (L) or right (R). 
\f0\b MOVEMENT_SIDE (0/L/R)
\f2\b0  
\f0\b \'a0
\f2\b0 records which side of the T maze the individual moved towards during the playback period. 
\f0\b START CALL(min)
\f2\b0  contains the information on the time it took an individual to initiate the call. 
\f0\b REMARKS
\f2\b0  contain crucial information, such as whether an animal stopped calling before the playback, which helps determine whether to retain the data during analysis. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \

\f2 This file was used for movement analysis and call characteristic change analysis across experiments. The relevant analysis and the figure can be found in the main manuscript under the Result, Locomotory response section along with the Figure 5a and Figure 5b.
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

