\pard\pardeftab720\sl337\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 EXPOSURE SPL(dB)
\f2\b0  is the information of the decibel experienced by the cricket at the choice point, which was constant at 70 dB across and within the experiment type. 
\f0\b MALE_SPL_PRE_EXPO(dB)\'a0 
\f2\b0 is the Sound Pressure Level (SPL) of a male, 5 min before the start of the playback. 
\f0\b MALE_SPL_POST_EXPO(dB) 
\f2\b0 is the Sound Pressure Level (SPL) of a male post the cessation of the playback. 
\f0\b CHIRP_RATE_PRE_EXPO_3min(s) 
\f2\b0 is the chirp rate of a male 3 min within call initiation. 
\f0\b CHIRP_RATE_PRE_EXPO_5min(s) 
\f2\b0 is the chirp rate of a male 5 min within call initiation. 
\f0\b CHIRP_RATE_PRE_EXPO_8min(s) 
\f2\b0 is the chirp rate of a male 8 min within call initiation. 
\f0\b CHIRP_RATE_POST_EXPO(s)\'a0 
\f2\b0 is the chirp rate of a male post-playback. 
\f0\b Call_NOCALL_DURING-EXPO 
\f2\b0 records in a binary form whether a male called during exposure, where 1 is denoted if a male called and 0 if a male didn\'92t call during playback. 
\f0\b Call_NOCALL_POST-EXPO
\f2\b0 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 records in a binary form whether a male called after the playback stopped. 1 was denoted if a male called and 0 if a male didn\'92t call. 
\f0\b SPEAKER_SIDE\'a0 
\f2\b0 refers to the side of the active speaker, which can be either left (L) or right (R).
\f0\b  MOVEMENT_SIDE (0/L/R)\'a0\'a0 
\f2\b0 records which side of the T maze the individual moved towards during the playback period. 
\f0\b Towards:1 
\f2\b0 convert the 
\f0\b MOVEMENT_SIDE 
\f2\b0 data into binary, where 1 is denoted if the speaker side and 
\f0\b MOVEMENT_SIDE 
\f2\b0 are the same.\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\b REMARKS 
\f2\b0 contain crucial information, such as whether an animal stopped calling before the playback, which helps determine whether to retain the data during analysis. 
\f0\b STOP CALL
\f2\b0  records
\f0\b  
\f2\b0 the time when the individual stops calling after playback. 
\f0\b START CALL
\f2\b0  records when an individual resumes calling again. 
\f0\b INTERMITTENT_CALLER_PRE_EXPO (0/1) 
\f2\b0 if an individual stopped calling for a continuous minute at least \'a0and resumed calling within 10 minutes of initiating call, it was classified as an intermittent caller. The data was logged in binary form, where\'a0 1 represents an intermittent caller and 0 represents a continuous caller. Similarly, 
\f0\b INTERMITTENT_CALLER_DURING_EXPO (0/1) 
\f2\b0 records this behaviour in the binary format during the playback period. 
\f0\b INTERMITTENT_CALLER_POST_EXPO (0/1)
\f2\b0  records intermittent calling after the playback stopped.
\f0\b  SILENT_DURING_EXPO (0/1)
\f2\b0  records the occurrence of males remaining silent during playback, where 0 is used for calling and 1 for a silent behavioural state for the entire playback duration. Similarly, 
\f0\b SILENT_POST_EXPO (0/1) 
\f2\b0 notes a prolonged silent behavioural state post-playback.
\f1 \
